# Path ownership for agent-runtime — the gate that lets a fixer work here without being able to
# edit its own governor. Same principle as homelab's CODEOWNERS and circles': OWN WHAT GOVERNS THE
# AGENT, NOT WHAT THE AGENT OPERATES ON.
#
# This repo is unusual: it IS the harness. `agent-base/` builds the image every ride runs inside,
# so a bad merge here does not break one project — it breaks the fleet's ability to fix itself.
# The fixer's scope is the harness SOURCES plus tests/; the things that decide what ships are owned.
# Narrowed 2026-10-13 (operator: homelab's rule work made the codeowner a non-blocker there, the
# platform repos were the ones still parking PRs — homelab ADR-154): the image definition and the
# root toolchain left the human gate, like homelab's own docker/ and devbox.json; a base-image
# or toolchain bump merges on CI + the reviewer bot, the dep files on deps-pin-guard's shape test.
#
# GitHub semantics: LAST matching pattern wins, and a pattern with NO owner REMOVES ownership.
# scripts/deps-pin-guard.sh reads this file at the merge-base to classify a mixed PR — only
# `*`, `/dir/` and `/path` shapes; anything fancier fails that guard closed.

# ── The build+publish path. `.github/workflows/` is governor-class HERE (unlike a stack repo,
# where a deploy workflow is ordinary product plumbing): these workflows push the image the whole
# fleet pulls, and open the deploy-pin PR into homelab.
/.github/                       @RasmusSoot

# ── Renovate's action-pin lane (homelab ADR-100 addendum / ADR-141, S9 #1990). Ownership is
# REPLACED, not dropped: `pin-only-lint` (homelab scripts/pin-only-lint.sh, run inside the
# required `ci` check) allows only verified action pin bumps (`uses: owner/repo@sha # tag`, the
# SHA resolved upstream to the tag's commit, pairs only, first-party refs frozen) through a PR;
# a real workflow edit takes the operator path straight to master, where the check does not run.
# Post-merge failures of push-only workflows roll back via the FU-1990 chain (drill passed on
# agent-coordinator, 2026-09-27). One-line revert: restore the owner below.
/.github/workflows/

# ── The recipes are the agent's own instructions — an agent able to edit them is not gated at all.
/.agents/                       @RasmusSoot

# ── The ownership file owns itself, or the first thing an agent can propose is its own ungating
# (homelab and oracle-fleet carry the same line for the same reason).
/CODEOWNERS                     @RasmusSoot

# Deliberately UNOWNED — CI (the unit tests) + the reviewer's approval are the gate:
#   agent-base/Dockerfile (un-owned 2026-10-13; owned 2026-08-11 → 2026-10-13), agent-base/agent-finalize,
#   agent-base/entrypoint.sh, agent-base/agent-storm-watchdog, tests/, scripts/ci.sh, docs/, README.md
# The dep files are un-owned with a REPLACEMENT owner: scripts/deps-pin-guard.sh in the required
# `ci` check passes only a version/hash diff of agent-base/devbox.{json,lock} (carved out
# 2026-08-11) and the root devbox.{json,lock} (un-owned 2026-10-13, guarded the same way). A
# non-version edit there is refused unless the PR also touches an OWNED path (the code owner
# reads it all); since 2026-10-13 a PR mixing them with other UN-owned paths gets the shape test
# instead of a refusal (openrouter-operator#83's fileset rule, agent-runtime#169 — under the
# narrowed ownership that mix is a worker adapting a bump, not two lanes in one PR).
